	<!--
		v203 - controls stay usable while a command is in flight: no greying out, 700 ms double-tap guard only,
		Sending... hint. Flame taps during ignition are queued (last tap wins) and applied once power is
		confirmed; other flame taps are debounced to one send. Page is www/fireplace3.html (page build 3). (UNTESTED)
		v202 - three-way Off / Pilot / On mode selector; last flame height restored (UNTESTED)
		Page is now www/fireplace3.html (page build 3). The Power row is replaced by one
		Off | Pilot | On selector: Off = UI_POWER_OFF, On = UI_POWER_ON, Pilot = UI_SET_PILOT.
		The driver remembers the last flame height while the fireplace is on and re-applies
		it after power comes on. Nothing on page open, refresh or reconnect turns anything on.
		
		v200 - uibutton + web view rebuild (UNTESTED on hardware and in Composer)
		=========================================================================
		The v120 relay proxy (relaysingle_gasfireplace_c4) is replaced by a
		uibutton proxy on binding 5001. The tile opens www/fireplace3.html in
		Navigator: a status header, an Off / Pilot / On mode selector and a 5-step
		flame level selector. The tile icon changes with the fireplace state:
		Off (fp_off), Pilot (fp_pilot), Flame1..Flame5 (flame1..flame5).

		Relay connections 5001/5002 and the relay notifications are gone; Network
		connection 6001 (TCP port 80) is unchanged. Changing proxy type means the
		device must be deleted and re-added in Composer.

		PACKAGE NAME: IntelliFire_driver.c4z, and <name> is the same slug. Navigator
		resolves controller://driver/IntelliFire_driver/... from it; if they do
		not match, Navigator hides the tile. The display name is <model>.

		PAGE FILE IS RENAMED EVERY PAGE RELEASE (fireplace1, fireplace2, ...)
		because Navigator caches controller:// pages. web_view_url below,
		PAGE_FILE / PAGE_BUILD in the Lua and the file in www/ must agree.

		Composer commands and actions (Set Pilot, Fireplace On/Off, Pilot On/Off,
		Refresh Status, Print Debug Info) are kept. Composer variables FIREPLACE_ON,
		PILOT_ON and FLAME_LEVEL are updated on state changes; the events Fireplace
		Turned On and Fireplace Turned Off fire on transitions only.

		Rollback points in git history: v120 (relay proxy) and v117 (thermostat).
		HTTP polling, SHA-256 signing, SendFireplaceCommand and the reconcile logic
		are unchanged from v120.
	-->
	<proxies qty="1">
		<proxy proxybindingid="5001" name="IntelliFire Fireplace" primary="True" image_source="c4z" small_image="icons/device_sm.png" large_image="icons/device_lg.png">uibutton</proxy>
	</proxies>

	<connections>
		<connection>
			<id>5001</id>
			<facing>6</facing>
			<connectionname>UIBUTTON</connectionname>
			<type>2</type>
			<consumer>False</consumer>
			<audiosource>False</audiosource>
			<videosource>False</videosource>
			<linelevel>False</linelevel>
			<classes>
				<class>
					<classname>UIBUTTON</classname>
				</class>
			</classes>
		</connection>
		<connection>
			<id>6001</id>
			<facing>1</facing>
			<connectionname>Network</connectionname>
			<type>4</type>
			<consumer>True</consumer>
			<audiosource>False</audiosource>
			<videosource>False</videosource>
			<linelevel>True</linelevel>
			<classes>
				<class>
					<classname>TCP</classname>
					<ports>
						<port>
							<number>80</number>
							<auto_connect>True</auto_connect>
							<monitor_connection>True</monitor_connection>
							<keep_connection>False</keep_connection>
						</port>
					</ports>
				</class>
			</classes>
		</connection>
	</connections>

